From: Benedek Kupper <kupper.benedek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: udc: nrf: ignore data done without a transfer

The USBD interrupt handler dereferenced the IN endpoint's first queued
buffer on every data done event (EPDATA or EP0DATADONE). When the driver
thread cancels the transfer after the host acknowledged its last packet,
but before the interrupt handler processes the event, the queue is empty
and the handler faults on a NULL buffer.

Seen on nRF52840 while the threads were starved for 400 ms and the host
reset the bus and issued control transfers: MPU fault, data access at
0x10, in usbd_in_packet_sent(). The event belongs to a transfer that no
longer exists: ignore it.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c b/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
index 50417eaab7d..deb0ea8901e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
@@ -471,6 +471,10 @@ static void usbd_in_packet_sent(uint8_t ep)
 	struct udc_ep_config *ep_cfg = udc_get_ep_cfg(udc_nrf_dev, ep);
 	struct net_buf *buf = udc_buf_peek(ep_cfg);
 
+	if (buf == NULL) {
+		return;
+	}
+
 	net_buf_pull(buf, usbd_ep_amount_get(ep));
 
 	if (buf->len) {
